import sys
p = sys.argv[1]
lines = open(p, encoding='utf-8').read().split('\n')
idx = [i for i, l in enumerate(lines) if l.startswith('| 642 |')]
assert len(idx) == 1
lines.insert(idx[0] + 1, "| 643 | 2026-10-24 | **Rhythm on the Home, part 2: groups 3 and 4.** RqStaff: a row on the staff with the rhythm chapter's renderer (time signature, bar lines, beams, dots, ties, an anacrusis; SrhFit / srhRaw), played and scored as in that chapter (on time and held for the note's length, srhScore); ties are merged (the tied-to note is not struck or tapped again); 'only' scores taps on chosen beats (the strong beats); the strong beat can sound accented. Group 3 'Bars and time signatures' (Questions: time-signatures drill): Bars and bar lines (how many bars?), The two numbers (2/4, 3/4, 4/4, C = 4/4; how many beats in a bar?), Strong and weak beats (4/4 strong-weak-medium-weak, 3/4 strong-weak-weak; tap only beat 1; hear 2, 3 or 4), Fill the bar (which note fills the box: crotchet to semibreve), The tie (one sound across the bar line; how long does the tied note last?). Group 4 'Rhythm patterns' (Questions: rhythm drill): Grouping quavers (beamed right? the 4/4 middle stays clear), A quaver alone (the quaver rest; which count?), The dotted crotchet (1½ beats, long-short), Before beat 1 (anacrusis; the last bar is often short too), Count, clap, play (which line did you hear?). Rows reused from the rhythm chapter (SRH_ROWS). Korean terms: 세로줄, 겹세로줄, 박자표, 센박, 여린박, 중강 (for the medium beat 3 in 4/4), 붙임줄, 빔, 8분쉼표, 점4분음표, 못갖춘마디. Group 5 (semiquavers, triplets, 6/8, 2/2, syncopation and swing) still to come; the renderer needs 6/8 and triplets first. Files: drills.html, drills.src.html, _workspace/concept-book-kit/sc/{patch665.py,rq2.jsx}. |")
open(p, 'w', encoding='utf-8').write('\n'.join(lines)); print('ok')
